<title>UK: Reuters eases back after H1 results.</title>
<headline>Reuters eases back after H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters Holdings Plc shares dipped on Wednesday as the news and financial information group said pre-tax profit fell three percent in the first half and announced a 200 million stg share buyback.</p>
<p>The stock, which has lately rebounded from its year's low of 555p set on July 10, was down 3p at 606-1/2 by 1020 GMT up, after being up 11p shortly before the announcement.</p>
<p>Analysts and dealers said the results had not provided enough of a positive surprise to allow the stock to build on its rally of recent sessions.</p>
</text>
